# interview purpose

Create EC2 Instances with Security Groups and Elastic IPs
Provision S3 Buckets with HTTP Endpoints
Set Up VPCs with Subnets and Route Tables
Create RDS Databases with Automatic Backups
Deploy Lambda Functions with API Gateway Integrations
Set Up Elastic Load Balancers and Auto Scaling for Web Applications
Deploy IAM Roles, Policies, and User Access Management


Assignment 1 – Secure Web Server
Task:
Create a web server that can be accessed by users over the internet.
Requirements
Create an EC2 instance.
Install Apache/Nginx.
Create a Security Group allowing only HTTP and SSH.
Verify the web page using the public IP.

Assignment 2 – Secure File Storage
Task:
Create secure cloud storage for company documents.
Requirements
Create an S3 bucket.
Enable Versioning.
Enable Server-Side Encryption.
Block Public Access.
Upload sample files.

Assignment 3 – Employee Access Management
Task:
The company has Developers and Testers.
Requirements
Create IAM Groups.
Create IAM Users.
Developers can manage EC2.
Testers can only view EC2.
Enable MFA.
Assignment 4 – Company Network

Task:
Design a secure AWS network.

Requirements
Create a VPC.
Create Public and Private Subnets.
Attach an Internet Gateway.
Configure Route Tables.
Launch EC2 in the Public Subnet.
Assignment 5 – Database Deployment

Task:
Deploy a MySQL database securely.

Requirements
Create an RDS MySQL instance.
Enable Automatic Backup.
Disable Public Access.
Allow only EC2 to connect.
Assignment 6 – High Availability

Task:
Deploy a highly available web application.

Requirements
Launch two EC2 instances.
Place them in different Availability Zones.
Configure an Application Load Balancer.
Test Load Balancing.
Assignment 7 – Auto Scaling

Task:
Your website traffic increases during office hours.

Requirements
Create an Auto Scaling Group.
Desired Capacity = 2
Maximum Capacity = 5
Scale when CPU > 70%.
Assignment 8 – Monitoring

Task:
Monitor your production server.

Requirements
Create a CloudWatch Alarm.
Trigger SNS Email Notification.
Alert when CPU > 80%.
Assignment 9 – Serverless Image Upload

Task:
Automatically process uploaded images.

Requirements
Create an S3 Bucket.
Create a Lambda Function.
Trigger Lambda when an image is uploaded.
Store log output in CloudWatch.
Assignment 10 – Public API

Task:
Create an API without managing servers.

Requirements
Create a Lambda Function.
Integrate with API Gateway.
Return JSON response.
